{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015FhveU6gvrLYziHR4gveRF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Prompts\n2\t\n3\tAppend-only, written by `.claude/hooks/log-prompt.sh`. Do not edit past entries.\n4\t\n5\t## 2026-09-27T23:10:50Z · 1a81e73e\n6\t\n7\t```text\n8\t/refine a docs/specs/SPEC.v1-todo-list-cli-mvp.md for creating a todo list app. Main objective is a simple setup but well integratable into CI with well set up test infrastructure using our ways of working for a scala pure fp cats style. The output should be colored and well structured, it should be possible to interface the todo list app with yaml and rich text directly. Configuration is pure cli args only, no env vars and no other config options. A local todo file in the current directory is the default path, create it when there is none, and on reads complain about a missing file or parameter.\n9\t\n10\tThese choices are settled, so write the spec:\n11\t- The human view is colored, structured terminal output. Rich text is a Markdown checklist the app imports and exports.\n12\t- YAML is the one store file, and the app imports and exports that same YAML.\n13\t- The MVP commands are add, list, done, and remove.\n14\t- CI is `just check`. Name that gate in the spec. The workflow file lands with the first code milestone.\n15\t```\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a81e73e-217d-414b-8c54-b62168eabfb9","uuid":"143f4784-4ecc-4c28-a5da-a6fd0717c429","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:10:56.793Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/isaiasbartelborth/Projects/hivemind/todo-list-cli/develop/docs/PROMPTS.md","content":"# Prompts\n\nAppend-only, written by `.claude/hooks/log-prompt.sh`. Do not edit past entries.\n\n## 2026-09-27T23:10:50Z · 1a81e73e\n\n```text\n/refine a docs/specs/SPEC.v1-todo-list-cli-mvp.md for creating a todo list app. Main objective is a simple setup but well integratable into CI with well set up test infrastructure using our ways of working for a scala pure fp cats style. The output should be colored and well structured, it should be possible to interface the todo list app with yaml and rich text directly. Configuration is pure cli args only, no env vars and no other config options. A local todo file in the current directory is the default path, create it when there is none, and on reads complain about a missing file or parameter.\n\nThese choices are settled, so write the spec:\n- The human view is colored, structured terminal output. Rich text is a Markdown checklist the app imports and exports.\n- YAML is the one store file, and the app imports and exports that same YAML.\n- The MVP commands are add, list, done, and remove.\n- CI is `just check`. Name that gate in the spec. The workflow file lands with the first code milestone.\n```\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}}}
